    - adding `firsts[0]` at `CN_TECH_MIN_GAMES - 1` games, a Core token's id (`def.is_token()`) and `"core-999"` (each at the floor) still gives `vec![SHIPPED_SETS[0]]`;
    - all of `firsts` at the floor gives an empty list.
- Run `cargo test -p jackioh-tools winrates`, `cargo test -p jackioh-cards c050_cn_tech`, `cargo test -p jackioh-cards c002_na_tech`, `cargo test -p jackioh-ai --features jackioh-engine/testkit`, then the harness's full `cargo test --workspace --features jackioh-engine/testkit,jackioh-engine/ts`.

**Done when.**

- [ ] The winrates R2386000 test passes. The cards R2386000 test failed before step 8 (output kept) and passes after.
- [ ] `win_rates.json`: `patch` is `v0.5.6b`, `source` is `provisional`, and there are rows for all seven shipped sets.
- [ ] The fragment exists and `classify --claims` passed in step 10.
- [ ] `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo jackioh catalog check`, `patches check`, `spec check` and `golden check` pass. `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` and the full cargo test pass, with `apps/web/src/wire` unchanged.
- [ ] The PR notes list the re-blessed seeds and why (CN Tech's or NA Tech's pick), the extra `plays` ids and why, and the stats files used.
- [ ] No extra worktree is left.

**Risks.**

- Replay: older versions keep `patches/win_rates/<version>.json`; don't touch them.
- Ladder bots' decks lean on the table (`crates/ai/src/deck.rs` `win_rate_weight`, strength > 0 only); AI and server tests register their own tables. If one fails on the new table, report it; never bend it.
- Hidden information is unchanged: the pick stays a hidden hand add.
- The daily `.github/workflows/winrates-refresh.yml` can now open a Fills refresh, and its PR text says "live games". That is wording only, and not ours to edit.
- A Fills refresh counts as the X's refresh. Training Grounds' pending release ships as v0.5.7, a new patch, so the live refresh stays open.

**Open questions.** None block the build; the owner approved the proposal over a live-only table. Two choices for R2386000 and the PR notes: a Fills refresh needs the input to cover every shipped set (rejected: filling only some), and it counts as the X's refresh (rejected: a live refresh following in the same X, which a provisional live-rule table could turn into a daily loop).

